    "methods_description": "Participants studied visually presented word lists, performed arithmetic distractor tasks, and then freely recalled words. Open-loop electrical stimulation was delivered to a single electrode (hippocampus or entorhinal cortex) during encoding on 20 of 25 lists, targeting alternating two-word blocks, with stimulation starting 200 ms before word onset and lasting 4.6 seconds. iEEG recordings were collected in monopolar and bipolar configurations using Blackrock and Medtronic systems, with voltage scaling applied to standardize units.",
